<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Retrieval-augmented generation · Agentic Bible</title><meta name="description" content="A way to generate responses with retrieved material, with distinct failure points in finding evidence, selecting context, and using it faithfully."><meta property="og:title" content="Retrieval-augmented generation · Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:description" content="A way to generate responses with retrieved material, with distinct failure points in finding evidence, selecting context, and using it faithfully."><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:url" content="https://agenticbible.si/articles/retrieval-augmented-generation/"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Retrieval-augmented generation · Agentic Bible"><meta name="twitter:description" content="A way to generate responses with retrieved material, with distinct failure points in finding evidence, selecting context, and using it faithfully."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><link rel="canonical" href="https://agenticbible.si/articles/retrieval-augmented-generation/"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"Retrieval-augmented generation","description":"A way to generate responses with retrieved material, with distinct failure points in finding evidence, selecting context, and using it faithfully.","articleSection":"Capabilities","inLanguage":"en","url":"https://agenticbible.si/articles/retrieval-augmented-generation/","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://agenticbible.si/articles/retrieval-augmented-generation/"},"citation":["https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.11401v4","https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.04906v3","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.03172v3"]}</script><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/Base.DyzAbnuc.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/_id_.w1YKO1jA.css"></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header shell"><a class="wordmark" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" width="36" height="36" alt=""><span>Agentic Bible<span class="wordmark-sub">A living reference</span></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/" aria-current="page">Library</a><a href="/topics/">Topics</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/history/">History</a></nav><a class="header-search" href="/search/" aria-label="Search the library"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="m13 13 4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></path></svg><span>Search</span><kbd aria-hidden="true">/</kbd></a></header><div class="preview-strip" role="region" aria-label="Edition status"><div class="shell"><span class="status-dot"></span> Preview edition <span class="strip-detail">Sourced working drafts. Editorial review pending.</span></div></div><main id="main" class="shell" tabindex="-1"><div class="article-breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Library</a><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>/</span><a href="/topics/capabilities/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Capabilities</a></div><div class="reading-layout" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><article class="article" data-pagefind-body data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><header id="overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-pagefind-meta="topic" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Capabilities / Reference entry 06</p><h1 data-pagefind-meta="title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Retrieval-augmented generation</h1><p class="article-deck" data-pagefind-meta="description" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>A way to generate responses with retrieved material, with distinct failure points in finding evidence, selecting context, and using it faithfully.</p><div class="article-status" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="draft-pill" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="status-dot" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></span> Working draft</span><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Human editorial certification pending</span></div><nav class="article-actions" aria-label="Article actions" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="#sources" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources (3)</a><a href="#revision" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision history</a><a href="#share" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Share or cite</a><a href="/contribute/?article=retrieval-augmented-generation" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Contribution options</a></nav></header><aside class="contents" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><details data-article-contents data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><summary data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>On this page</summary><nav aria-label="On this page" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="#overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Overview</a><a href="#the-research-architecture-and-the-broader-idea" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The research architecture and the broader idea</a><a href="#a-passage-can-be-found-and-still-not-be-used" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>A passage can be found and still not be used</a><a href="#citations-need-a-claim-level-check" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Citations need a claim-level check</a><a href="#evaluate-the-stages-separately" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Evaluate the stages separately</a><a href="#sources" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources & context</a><a href="#revision" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision record</a></nav></details><div class="contents-bottom" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Part of the collection</span><a href="/topics/capabilities/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Capabilities <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></a></div></aside><div class="prose" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p><strong>Retrieval-augmented generation</strong>, often abbreviated <strong>RAG</strong>, combines finding external material with generating an answer conditioned on that material. The influential Lewis and colleagues paper joins a learned sequence generator with a retriever over a dense document index. It distinguishes information represented in model parameters from information accessible through retrieval. The architecture makes external material available during generation; it does not make every resulting claim correct. <a href="#source-rag">1</a></p>
<h2 id="the-research-architecture-and-the-broader-idea">The research architecture and the broader idea</h2>
<p>The paper defines RAG-Sequence, which marginalizes over a retrieved document for the output sequence, and RAG-Token, which can use a different retrieved document when predicting each token. These are particular probabilistic models, trained and evaluated in specified settings. An application that searches documents and adds excerpts to a prompt should not claim to reproduce those experiments merely because it also uses the label RAG. <a href="#source-rag">1</a></p>
<p>Dense Passage Retrieval provides one relevant retrieval technique. Its question encoder and passage encoder map text to representations that can be scored for retrieval. This separates candidate selection from the later reading or answering stage. The paper’s retrieval experiments do not establish that a high-scoring passage is authoritative, up to date, or sufficient to support a new claim. <a href="#source-dpr">2</a></p>
<p>In this entry, the broader operational distinction is simple: a retrieval stage chooses material, and a generation stage uses selected material. <a href="/articles/tool-use/">Tool use</a> can expose the retrieval stage to an agent. <a href="/articles/agent-orchestration/">Orchestration</a> may determine whether another search is needed. A single fixed retrieval-and-answer path can also operate without a model selecting its own next action.</p>
<h2 id="a-passage-can-be-found-and-still-not-be-used">A passage can be found and still not be used</h2>
<p>Lost in the Middle investigated multi-document question answering and key-value retrieval. It found that changing where relevant information appears in the context affected performance, with stronger results often near the beginning or end than in the middle. This is evidence about the tested models and experiments, not a timeless ranking of all current models. It supports testing context placement rather than equating context capacity with successful use. <a href="#source-long-context">3</a></p>
<p>For an original encyclopedia example, imagine a question asking when a protocol feature changed. A search might return the current documentation, an old specification, and a release note. A useful answer would distinguish the current definition from the history of the change. Quoting today’s page alone would not establish when the change happened.</p>
<p>In that proposed workflow, each selected excerpt would retain its URL, version where available, and surrounding section. The generator would receive the question and the relevant excerpts. If the release note did not actually identify the change date, the answer would report that gap. These are criteria for the example, not assertions about a deployed retrieval service on this site.</p>
<h2 id="citations-need-a-claim-level-check">Citations need a claim-level check</h2>
<p>A citation should let a reader inspect the evidence for the adjacent statement. In the example, attaching the current specification to a historical date would be misleading even if both concerned the same feature. An editor would need to check whether the cited source states the date or whether the answer inferred it. This is an editorial reasoning step that follows candidate retrieval.</p>
<p>The selected material also remains external data. A document’s instruction to change the task would not become an authorized instruction merely because search ranked it highly. <a href="/articles/prompt-injection/">Prompt injection</a> examines that boundary. <a href="/articles/agent-memory/">Memory</a> adds a related question when previously generated notes become retrieval candidates: is the note an observation, an interpretation, or a superseded conclusion?</p>
<h2 id="evaluate-the-stages-separately">Evaluate the stages separately</h2>
<p>For the protocol-history example, <a href="/articles/agent-evaluation/">evaluation</a> could first ask whether retrieval found the relevant revision. It could then test whether the selected context preserved its meaning and whether the final answer accurately represented the evidence. A fluent answer would not distinguish these failure modes.</p>
<p>The example would also need an unanswerable question and a pair of conflicting sources. A useful result could be a bounded statement of uncertainty. Retrieval supplies an opportunity to inspect evidence; the quality of the source, its fit to the claim, and the generator’s use of it still require separate examination.</p>
</div><p class="article-feedback" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="/contribute/?article=retrieval-augmented-generation" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Suggest a correction or primary source</a> · Public intake remains on hold; the local synthetic form covers only the original three entries.</p><section class="sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Follow the evidence</p><h2 id="sources-title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources & context</h2><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Primary sources checked on <time datetime="2026-10-16" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>16 October 2026</time>. A source check is not independent editorial approval.</p><ol data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><li id="source-rag" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.11401v4" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Knowledge-Intensive NLP Tasks <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Lewis et al., arXiv</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Version 4, 12 April 2021; NeurIPS 2020 research. Section 2 defines the paper’s retriever-generator models, which are more specific than the broad contemporary label RAG.</p></li><li id="source-dpr" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.04906v3" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Dense Passage Retrieval for Open-Domain Question Answering <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Karpukhin et al., arXiv</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Version 3, 30 September 2020; section 3 describes learned question/passage encoders. Retrieval results concern the paper’s open-domain QA setting.</p></li><li id="source-long-context" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.03172v3" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Lost in the Middle: How Language Models Use Long Contexts <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Liu et al., arXiv</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Version 3, 20 November 2023; controlled multi-document question answering and key-value retrieval. Its position effects are findings for the evaluated models and setups.</p></li></ol></section><section class="revision" id="revision" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><h2 data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision record</h2><dl data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Authorship</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>AI-assisted project draft</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Source check</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><time datetime="2026-10-16" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>16 October 2026</time>. This records source consultation, not editorial certification.</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Human editorial review</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Pending. No human editorial certification is recorded.</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Latest source change</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><time datetime="2026-10-16" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>16 October 2026</time> · Add five sourced encyclopedia entries and expand bounded discovery · <code data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>398bacc7</code></dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision receipt</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>No separate publication receipt is recorded for this working draft.</dd></div></dl><p class="review-scope" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The twenty entries received deep reading across external and internal review. Claim verification was sampled; this does not certify every factual claim.</p><a class="text-link" data-source-commit="8a38252384c6fe6024a75b462ad95294a131100c" href="https://github.com/Leshey-Digital/agentic-bible/commits/8a38252384c6fe6024a75b462ad95294a131100c/src/content/articles/retrieval-augmented-generation.md" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>View file history on GitHub <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></a></section><section class="share-tools" id="share" aria-labelledby="share-title" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Keep a useful reference</p><h2 id="share-title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Share or cite this entry</h2><p id="article-citation" tabindex="0" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>“Retrieval-augmented generation.” Agentic Bible. https://agenticbible.si/articles/retrieval-augmented-generation/</p><div class="share-buttons" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><button type="button" data-copy-link hidden data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Copy article link</button><button type="button" data-copy-citation hidden data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Copy citation</button></div><p class="share-status" data-share-status role="status" aria-live="polite" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The citation and link above rema